  "term": "pragmatism",
  "definition": "In this historical logical sense, pragmatism is the principle of approaching logical questions by their purpose: finding the general conditions of truth. It guides inquiry toward ways of analyzing propositions that help solve that problem and away from distinctions that do not.",
